  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \r\rSuds proforma    \rCovering letter with heritage statement\r00-DR-04 1010\r00-DR-04 3070\r00-DR-04 3071\r00-DR-04 2010\r00-DR-01 1000\r00-DR-00 1010\r00-DR-00 3070\r00-DR-00 3071\r00-DR-00 2010\r00-DR-02 0011 (Proposed Block Plan)\r00-DR-02 0000 (Site Location Plan)\r00-DR-02 0010 (Existing Block Plan)\rHighway safety impact proforma    \rEnvironmental Noise Assessment dated 8th December 2025\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "No more than 10% of the glazed area of the ground floor frontage of the eye clinic hereby permitted shall be obscured (i.e. by items fixed directly to the glazing which prevent visual permeability) in anyway.\r\rReason: In order to maintain active frontages and visual amenity in accordance with DMD 40 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) regarding Ground Floor Frontages.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification, the premises shall only be used as a Veterinary clinic (Use Class E (e)) and no other purpose outside of Class E (e) unless written permission is otherwise granted.\r\rReason: To prevent the introduction uses that would give rise to conditions prejudicial to the character of the area.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, the development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved acoustic details as set out in (ref: Environmental Noise Assessment dated 8th December 2025). \r\rReason: To protect the local amenity from noise and disturbance\r"
  ],
